WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.470
At a French bakery, ask for «un gâteau».

2
00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.600
You walk out with the whole cake.

3
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.140
Ask for «du gâteau», and you get a slice.

4
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.660
And English 'I eat bread'?

5
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.610
Copy it word for word into French,

6
00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:14.860
and it's wrong.

7
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:19.350
Then that little «du» sometimes
shrinks to a tiny «de».

8
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.850
When? So why can't you
just say 'I eat bread',

9
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:25.030
and when does 'some' shrink?

10
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:28.680
In this mission, you'll slice
cakes and pizzas into French.

11
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.240
Then you'll flip three
switches on one sentence,

12
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.690
and predict what happens to its article.

13
00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.850
Your mission: crack when French says «du»,

14
00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.920
and when it shrinks to «de».
